---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Fictional History Archive">
  <div class="border-b-2 border-archive-border pb-4 mb-8">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-archive-paper mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-archive-muted">
      Data Integrity & Temporal Security Protocol
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-archive-surface border border-archive-border p-8 space-y-6 text-archive-paper font-serif leading-relaxed">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-archive-accent font-sans">Last Updated: [Current Timeline]</p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">1. Collection of Multiversal Data</h2>
    <p>
      The Fictional History Archive is committed to preserving the anonymity and temporal integrity of all submitting archivists. We do not track localized Earth-prime IP addresses, nor do we employ tracking chronitons that might reveal your current point of origin in the space-time continuum.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">2. Use of Archival Records</h2>
    <p>
      Any historical data submitted to the Archive is utilized solely for the purpose of maintaining a comprehensive, multiversal historical record. The Archive will not sell, trade, or otherwise barter your dimensional coordinates to temporal enforcement agencies, rogue synthetics, or intergalactic megacorporations.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">3. Local Storage and Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      To ensure the stability of your microfilm viewing experience, the Archive may utilize localized data caches (colloquially known in Earth-prime as "cookies"). These are strictly functional and serve to maintain your preferred atmospheric settings and multiversal viewing preferences across sessions.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">4. Redaction Requests</h2>
    <p>
      If an entity, collective consciousness, or authorized temporal authority believes their history has been erroneously cataloged or represents an active threat to a localized reality, redaction requests may be submitted to the Archive's central administration. Please note that paradoxes resulting from such redactions are solely the responsibility of the requesting party.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl mt-8 mb-4">5. Modifications to the Protocol</h2>
    <p>
      The Archive reserves the right to update this protocol should structural changes occur within the underlying fabric of reality. Archivists are encouraged to review these protocols periodically, or whenever they transition between major timeline branches.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
